4 Industrial promotion policy
4.1 «Positive Non-Intervention» until 1997
The colonial government, contrary to the governments
of other newly industrialised countries in Asia, largely refrained from promoting businesses by loans or subsidies or from raising taxes. The responsibility of the State was in theory restricted to providing an infrastructural
framework, an efficient civil service and keeping law and order. Although in reality Hong Kong's government
played a more active role (Yeh & Ng 1994: 460ff,
